      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T20:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Intended, per the operator decision recorded on starving-sphalerite-skua (2026-11-19): signing is not gated on an allowed identity, and an off-keyring signature that is sound against its own key and binds its event is an identity finding that does not fail the enforced check. Patch set 2 records this policy and its consequence as an amendment to ADR 0045 and in the verify-identity help. A signature that does not verify against its own key, or does not bind its event, still fails as bad-signature (tests test_signature_over_other_bytes_is_bad_signature and test_sound_signature_for_another_event_is_bad_signature).",
